  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_4ba30d7ed17945d186d4a6154b95a7e3",
      "statement": "PSP-Connector exposes a provider SPI via two abstract classes, PaymentServiceProvider and RefundServiceProvider, whose default method bodies throw RuntimeException('METHOD_NOT_SUPPORTED'), making each method opt-in so a gateway implementation only overrides the operations it supports.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/PaymentServiceProvider.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:6b61f0b68dd7ad67033a45f032f98d1885c44e08e8ea94c5b13754eb52754e89"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/RefundServiceProvider.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:c67346406c1342f608f091b1667e53a8a41796a1db00235bf71029f9d03be061"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_60cc1ebf6b3744159111bb564928e7db",
      "statement": "At bootstrap, Main instantiates OnecommPaymentServiceProvider (with PSP id and a dedicated verify-card merchant) and OnecommRefundServiceProvider and injects them into handler classes via static fields, so the HTTP handler layer is provider-agnostic and never references Onecomm directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/Main.java#L105-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44f7aa91f826941f36b15f5d01b9c63b0be738aa266cb0fcd72a439ffab94c56:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3622a6c7c74f4d7dbe2b4081cc4fe5cc",
      "statement": "OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.paymentPurchase inserts an initial payment record via PaymentService.insert, then for domestic transactions runs an FSP-Go fraud check (Fraud.checkFraud) before calling OnecommGateway.verifyCard, which builds signed request parameters and calls the Onecomm payment service.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommGateway.java#L48-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64c2e8cc27b2e0522440278be7928640eb8f5229d28c8eda419af42d9e4f4b90:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L191-L335",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a25b71c855af2fa45919146d8479f36b3dd206cbe8c6593077ec12a067cb44ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f1f36182665d49f9862032c0b7465af5",
      "statement": "When a Onecomm payment response is in AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED state, the provider creates an authorization record (AuthorizationService.insert) carrying the PSP authorization id and OTP approval URL, and includes it in the returned payment data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L518-L551",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b815c52d67c6e36e4cd221848268bc0a0d77552e4add3036edb658a9e89eb78a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_124bd668e27b44bab7724a1edcc12594",
      "statement": "OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.applePayNapasPaymentPurchase handles Apple Pay purchases routed through NAPAS, always executing a domestic fraud check and passing Apple Pay specific fields (payment_method, payment_data_decrypt, create_token, bank_id) to OnecommGateway.verifyCard, then recording paygate=applepay_napas in the txn extension data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L344-L504",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26f8e5e50d12942bdeb41d4d1de3d79ad9fd781a606081227bb9e4f761ed1462:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fa292d7c9c92474da32a056d3537d310",
      "statement": "The standard refund flow in OnecommRefundServiceProvider.paymentRefund decides auto vs manual via RefundRule.isManual, which encodes bank-specific rules: BIDV auto within 180 days, MBBank auto only when mbbank_txn_info.bank_request_id exists, AnBinhBank auto only same-day and full amount, NAPAS banks auto within 300 days, and VNPTMoney/VietinBank auto within 90 days.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/common/rulerefund/RefundRule.java#L25-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:227079856e80ae40345e26b4fbcfda93ee90f57b20550a738eed5312666fc7e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommRefundServiceProvider.java#L42-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93ad2666af6cb4f82697b9a0259c25ebdfd05c4d0c6ba83afcd8e1d706d60c10:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8bcda3a5a3546279a9fdd77ecb95008",
      "statement": "Auto refunds insert a PENDING refund record in RefundDB, call OnecommGateway.refundExtend, and map Onecomm response codes 200 to FAILED (bank declined), 300 to PENDING, and 400 to APPROVED before updating the refund record; manual refunds skip the gateway call and instead write an approved record to both OnecommDB (status 400) and RefundDB with process_type=manual.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommRefundServiceProvider.java#L357-L439",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2787ba81f817ff4409e6da8dd245f40a429683804a54c606b321785d78745a0d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommRefundServiceProvider.java#L96-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a9f471b7a9472b63781918e2428c27749e5ba38f9f89889dc5030280e033985:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b03bdbae41864350bf199c53dc2f1737",
      "statement": "OnecommRefundServiceProvider.updateRefund lets an MSP transition a pending refund to approved or failed, enforcing a strict state machine: refunds already in a terminal state (approved/failed) cannot be changed, approval requires an existing Onecomm refund transaction log, a refund already approved upstream (status 400) cannot be failed, and successful transitions move the Onecomm log to 400 (approved) or 200 (failed).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommRefundServiceProvider.java#L238-L354",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef51f27f7428a81df95c3abc95a4784a084d879265a65d4ae2f2551d194355a6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_40c3dd9fd8c04014bcf0b4c091d1b3ec",
      "statement": "OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.query resolves the reference to a payment via PspConnectorDB, cross-checks the transaction in Payment2DB, and for NAPAS-eligible banks (matching the napas.bank property) queries the NAPAS gateway via NapasGateway.query for real-time status; unsupported banks return vpc_DRExists=NA.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L815-L866",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7eef80108a852ea25e87e672e23fb6235fdebe5a1d27367b462f5d79f14e7727:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28740731b69a42b293a1e5416bad4c87",
      "statement": "Provider and refund behavior is driven by app.properties configuration: onepay.psp.id sets the provider id, verify_card.* supplies the dedicated verification merchant credentials, refund.bank.<bankId> sets each bank's refund process type (auto/manual), and napas.bank lists NAPAS-eligible bank ids as a regex.",
